.TH INGAUGE 1 "September 2026" "ingauge 0.4.30" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
ingauge \- observe and forecast local inference capacity
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ingauge
.RI [ OPTIONS ]
.RI [ COMMAND ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B ingauge
is an inference-capacity observability and forecasting tool. It discovers
capacity providers on the local system, probes them for current capacity,
stores timestamped observations in a SQLite database, and projects upcoming
capacity events.
.PP
Running
.B ingauge
without a command is equivalent to
.BR "ingauge status" ;
when no provider is configured and both stdin and stdout are terminals, an
interactive setup garage opens instead.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-\-json
Emit machine-readable JSON instead of styled human output. Global; valid on
every command.
.TP
.BI \-\-config " PATH"
Load configuration from
.IR PATH .
When absent, the configuration is resolved from the default config location.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show help.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Show version.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B status
.RB [ \-\-refresh ]
Show current capacity and upcoming events. With
.BR \-\-refresh ,
re-probe providers instead of serving cached state.
.TP
.B providers
List configured capacity targets.
.TP
.B discover
.RB [ \-\-harness\-directory " " \fIPATH\fR ]
Discover providers, routers, and harnesses on this system.
.TP
.B probe
Probe every enabled target now and record the observations.
.TP
.B history
.RB [ \-\-provider " " \fINAME\fR ]
.RB [ \-\-model " " \fINAME\fR ]
.RB [ \-\-since " " \fITIMESTAMP\fR ]
.RB [ \-\-limit " " \fIN\fR ]
Query timestamped capacity observations. Filters by provider, model, and
earliest timestamp; limits the number of rows (default 1000).
.TP
.B forecast
.RB [ \-\-provider " " \fINAME\fR ]
.RB [ \-\-model " " \fINAME\fR ]
Forecast consumption from stored observations.
.TP
.B next
Show the next projected capacity events.
.TP
.B health
Report daemon heartbeat health.
.TP
.B daemon
Run continuous capacity observation.
.TP
.BI config " COMMAND"
Validate configuration, or open the interactive provider configuration garage.
.RS
.TP
.B validate
Validate the configuration file.
.TP
.B tui
Open the interactive provider configuration garage.
.RE
.TP
.BI db " COMMAND"
Maintain the capacity database.
.RS
.TP
.B migrate
Apply schema migrations.
.TP
.B integrity
Check database integrity.
.TP
.B checkpoint
Run a database checkpoint.
.TP
.BI backup " OUTPUT"
Back up the database to
.IR OUTPUT .
.RE
.TP
.BI export " COMMAND"
Export capacity data to another system.
.RS
.TP
.BI padagonia " \-\-output " \fIPATH\fR " [\-\-since " \fITIMESTAMP\fR ]
Export observations in the Padagonia format.
.RE
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 3
Configuration error.
.TP
.B 4
Provider error.
.TP
.B 5
Storage, I/O, or serialization error.
.PP
With
.BR \-\-json ,
errors are reported on stderr as a JSON envelope with
.B schema_version
and
.B errors
fields.
.SH FILES
.TP
.B $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/ingauge/ingauge.toml
Per-user configuration.
.TP
SQLite history database
Timestamped capacity observations, per the configured database path.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B NO_COLOR
Disable styled output.
.TP
.B INGAUGE_NO_ANIMATION
Disable animation (reduced motion).
.TP
.B RUST_LOG
Controls tracing output.
.SH SECURITY
Remote endpoints require HTTPS. Credentials are resolved from environment
variables named in configuration and are never persisted.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
# Show current capacity (default command)
ingauge

# Machine-readable status for automation
ingauge --json status

# Discover local providers, then probe every enabled target
ingauge discover
ingauge probe

# Observations for one provider, last 50 rows
ingauge history --provider ollama --limit 50

# Forecast consumption and show upcoming events
ingauge forecast --provider ollama
ingauge next

# Validate the configuration and back up the database
ingauge config validate
ingauge db backup /tmp/ingauge-backup.db

# Run the continuous observer in the background
ingauge daemon
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
Full configuration reference:
.BR ingauge.example.toml
in the source tree.
